From: ZCode <agent@local>
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: brightness 0 turns the panel off, not to BL_MIN

sweet_bl_level() mapped brightness 0 to SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN (7), and
sweet_dsi_level() clamped every nonzero-or-zero value back up to that
minimum - so "display off" kept the panel lit at its lowest level and
the lock screen's last elements (the bottom bar) stayed visible, which
the user saw as "a progress bar appears when the screen goes off".
Allow true zero: brightness 0 sends panel level 0 (backlight off);
a nonzero value below SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN still clamps to the minimum.
---
 a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp | 10 ++++++++----
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -88,6 +88,9 @@ sweet_bl_level(uint32_t frac)
 sweet_bl_level(uint32_t frac)
 {
+	if (frac == 0) {
+		return 0;   /* display off: the backlight goes truly off, not to the panel's minimum */
+	}
 	return SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN + (uint32_t)((uint64_t)(SWEET_PANEL_BL_MAX - SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN) * frac * frac /
 	           (65536ULL * 65536ULL));
 }
@@ -150,7 +153,7 @@ static bool
 sweet_dsi_level(uint32_t level, bool log)
 {
-	level = level < SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN ? SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN :
+	level = level != 0 && level < SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN ? SWEET_PANEL_BL_MIN :
 	    (level > SWEET_PANEL_BL_MAX ? SWEET_PANEL_BL_MAX : level);
 	/* header: word count 3, 0, DCS long write 0x39, last + long; payload 51 hi lo, pad ff */
 	uint32_t cmd[2] = {0xc0390003u,
